It occurred to me when looking back at this thread
for any new articles, that NetHack needs (riiight)
your basic piebald cockatrice, whose corpse, when
applied to generic dragon scales, produces David
Dragon's Scales of Many Colors, an armor that has a
(say) 80% chance of responding with the appropriate
defensive response to any attack that _any_ dragon
scale mail might rebuff.

That might sound low, but consider that it would
apply to multiple simultaneous attacks against the
PC, and it might be a handy armor variety indeed,
giving a 64% chance of successfully rebuffing two
simultaneous different attacks, (say, acid and
disintegration), a ~51% chance of successfully
rebuffing three, etc.

There's lots of chances for other fun armors from
cocktrice stoning of animal or plant derived armors,
too.

For example, padded armor or padded gloves could
become pumice armor or gloves, very light but not
very strong.

For example, any stoned boots should be usable to
walk on lava, but with the disadvantage that they
get heavier with each step while on lave, as molten
stone congeals onto the boots, and only slowly
lighter after stepping off of lava, as each step
crumbles loose some of the accretion.

OTOH, if foolishly worn across water, the PC wearing
them, should, of course, be caused to "sink like a
stone", having a much worstened chance of surviving
than in even iron shoes.

